WEBVTT

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.838
We were adults before we were born.

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:06.339
What does that mean?

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:09.134
No access to memories before birth.

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:12.011
Things we have to forget to remember them.

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:13.346
I don't get it.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.349
Data about me not being me.

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:18.935
Impaired retention of self-identity.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.061
Who's that?

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:23.940
The answers to age-old questions
suddenly pop into someone's head.

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:27.318
Prenatal memories are being formed.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:29.863
You're our descendants.

00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:31.156
Mama.

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:35.493
We accept as our progeny those who arrive
at the answer to this question.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:38.997
-Mommy?
-New is old and old is new.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:39.956
Num-num?

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.834
Me before I was born.

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:46.004
The past is mostly shaped by the future.

00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:47.964
Memories of birth.

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:49.841
GOJIRA

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.385
The birth of someone who's not me.

00:00:57.265 --> 00:00:59.976
-Ready?
-Ready?

00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:08.860
What's that?

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.619
Pelops II!

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:21.039
You were out for two minutes this time.

00:01:21.122 --> 00:01:22.248
Is it just you now?

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:25.710
My rivals and I came to an agreement
through discussion.

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:27.212
Are they gone?

00:01:27.295 --> 00:01:29.631
They coexist inside me.

00:01:29.714 --> 00:01:33.760
Sorry to spoil your reunion,
but the Catastrophe is closing in.

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:40.266
About that, I found an unfinished task
from 50 years ago in the calculator.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.311
A task by Ashihara
who created the Archetype.

00:01:43.394 --> 00:01:44.270
Why a ship?

00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:48.691
Probably because it symbolizes a task
that was suspended before it exploded.

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:51.528
Is there more to the task then?

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:55.323
Professor Ashihara was searching
for a way to prevent the Catastrophe.

00:01:55.406 --> 00:01:58.660
He must have also been
calculating the method.

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:03.790
A code for the Orthogonal Diagonalizer
to prevent the Catastrophe?

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:05.500
Will you check it out?

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:06.668
I'd be happy to.

00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:15.343
Twenty minutes to the estimated time.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:16.886
03, proceeding.

00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:26.855
Good luck, 03.

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:28.648
The next bunch is coming.

00:02:30.358 --> 00:02:33.486
02, this is 01. Prepare to fire.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:34.904
Fire.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.160
Oh, Great Buddha.

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:42.370
Forward, clear. Let's speed up.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.959
A hill on the highway?

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:50.920
Who cares? Keep going!

00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:30.937
Commencing blockade.

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:34.023
Don't let it enter SHIVA.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.567
Non-security staff, evacuate immediately.

00:04:36.651 --> 00:04:39.988
Out the north gate, not the south.
There's no time.

00:04:40.071 --> 00:04:43.616
Is it here to get back Prometheus' fire?

00:04:55.878 --> 00:04:58.548
The monkey prevails?

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.931
Swim…

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:12.645
I see.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:16.816
The configuration
in the notebook is everywhere.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.447
He must have been using the Archetype
to stop the growth of the Singular Point.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.073
I knew it!

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:29.746
The task might give us the code
we need for the Orthogonal Diagonalizer.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.958
-How about fixing this sunken ship?
-What?

00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:37.253
Yes. If we can restart the task.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.422
But how can it be fixed?

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:40.673
Let me try.

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:48.806
In there…

00:05:52.268 --> 00:05:55.563
We're finished if they attack us.

00:05:55.646 --> 00:05:58.524
This is the crossroads.

00:06:01.235 --> 00:06:02.445
There.

00:06:14.832 --> 00:06:15.666
Thanks.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.086
You're welcome.

00:06:27.762 --> 00:06:28.679
Okay.

00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:34.560
Can you do it?

00:06:34.644 --> 00:06:36.104
I'm ready to go.

00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:39.315
Here they come.

00:06:41.275 --> 00:06:43.069
Behind the building to the right.

00:06:52.036 --> 00:06:54.372
Go left at the fork ahead.

00:06:54.455 --> 00:06:57.208
Sorry, but this is where we part ways.
Good luck.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:27.447
There are so many of them.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:28.406
Haberu!

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:30.741
Yes?

00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:34.745
A jump ramp just when we need it!

00:07:34.829 --> 00:07:37.748
Go before they catch up to us!

00:07:38.749 --> 00:07:40.251
Can you do it, Jet Jaguar?

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:41.502
I'll fly.

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:53.723
What a great view!

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.314
I'll fly!

00:08:03.232 --> 00:08:05.318
The output isn't stable.

00:08:05.401 --> 00:08:06.903
We need more lift!

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:07.904
Haberu!

00:08:12.783 --> 00:08:16.037
Fly!

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.588
Haberu!

00:08:35.348 --> 00:08:37.099
There we go.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:39.101
Pelops II, how's it going?

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.103
It's looking good.

00:08:46.108 --> 00:08:47.527
Twenty minutes?

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.486
What?

00:08:48.569 --> 00:08:50.446
Estimated time until the Catastrophe.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:51.864
Twenty minutes?

00:08:51.948 --> 00:08:53.115
Pelops II, can you hurry?

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:54.659
We have a problem.

00:08:54.742 --> 00:08:57.912
The Catastrophe is too close
to execute the calculation.

00:08:57.995 --> 00:08:59.455
Oh, no…

00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:00.623
Do you have any ideas?

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:05.836
Yes. I have a suggestion.
What about heading to the past?

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:06.796
Past?

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:10.883
Ashihara's task is still linked
to 50 years ago.

00:09:10.967 --> 00:09:14.595
The calculation can be extended
toward the past, in theory.

00:09:19.517 --> 00:09:20.643
What is it?

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:21.686
It's here.

00:09:33.781 --> 00:09:35.116
Five more minutes.

00:09:35.199 --> 00:09:36.450
I remember.

00:09:37.159 --> 00:09:38.703
I forgot something.

00:09:38.786 --> 00:09:40.079
Forgot what?

00:09:40.162 --> 00:09:42.456
I remember I forgot something.

00:09:44.542 --> 00:09:45.459
They're coming.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.937
Go behind a building!

00:10:10.568 --> 00:10:12.028
Why aren't they attacking?

00:10:23.831 --> 00:10:25.249
Godzilla?

00:10:30.838 --> 00:10:32.381
Dodge it, Jet Jaguar!

00:10:45.686 --> 00:10:48.230
Two minutes left. Don't get too far away.

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:49.357
I'm falling.

00:11:12.046 --> 00:11:13.089
Darn it!

00:11:13.589 --> 00:11:14.715
Danger!

00:11:31.148 --> 00:11:32.066
It's coming.

00:11:32.149 --> 00:11:34.151
-Pelops II.
-I'm ready.

00:11:34.235 --> 00:11:37.905
Heading to the past to calculate the code.

00:11:44.495 --> 00:11:46.163
Smooth sailing!

00:11:55.714 --> 00:11:58.676
It's going to destroy SHIVA
to get back the Singular Point.

00:11:58.759 --> 00:11:59.760
Pelops II?

00:11:59.844 --> 00:12:03.013
The calculation is moving along,
but you should all be leaving now.

00:12:03.097 --> 00:12:04.265
Staying any longer would be dangerous.

00:12:04.348 --> 00:12:05.933
But the code…

00:12:07.601 --> 00:12:09.770
I'll send it to you when I have it.

00:12:09.854 --> 00:12:15.025
That's right. Preventing the Catastrophe
would be meaningless if we're dead.

00:12:15.109 --> 00:12:16.360
What about you?

00:12:16.444 --> 00:12:20.614
I'll send my backup data
with the code if anything happens.

00:12:22.533 --> 00:12:24.118
-Let's go.
-We're counting on you.

00:12:24.201 --> 00:12:27.371
You got it. Be careful!

00:12:27.997 --> 00:12:30.249
If SHIVA gets destroyed
before we get the code…

00:12:30.332 --> 00:12:34.003
It's just attacking the exterior.
It won't easily…

00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:35.629
Pelops II, you okay?

00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:39.008
I felt it, but there's no influence
on the calculation.

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:41.552
I'm almost at the result.

00:12:42.887 --> 00:12:44.263
There's the answer!

00:12:45.473 --> 00:12:47.516
This is the answer?

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:55.983
Pelops II!

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.157
Jet Jaguar, how much time left?

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.742
Seventeen more seconds.

00:13:12.041 --> 00:13:13.792
Eight seconds. Seven.

00:13:13.876 --> 00:13:16.045
Six. Five.

00:13:16.128 --> 00:13:19.632
Four. Three. Two. One.

00:13:23.928 --> 00:13:24.803
The code?

00:13:24.887 --> 00:13:26.180
It's not here yet.

00:13:26.263 --> 00:13:28.682
Find it! It should be here!

00:13:28.766 --> 00:13:31.060
I can't find it. No new messages.

00:13:41.028 --> 00:13:42.196
Jet Jaguar!

00:13:42.279 --> 00:13:43.197
I got you.

00:13:46.659 --> 00:13:52.873
I checked the light, sound, heat,
wind velocity, humidity, and temperature

00:13:52.957 --> 00:13:55.543
but didn't find any relevant signals.

00:13:55.626 --> 00:13:56.961
I can't fly anymore.

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:07.930
Jet Jaguar!

00:14:26.782 --> 00:14:28.826
The code doesn't exist?

00:14:28.909 --> 00:14:34.623
There's no code for the Orthogonal
Diagonalizer to prevent the Catastrophe.

00:14:34.707 --> 00:14:39.295
We've exhausted all our options.
There's nothing else we can do.

00:14:42.047 --> 00:14:44.675
This song again? Where is it coming from?

00:14:44.758 --> 00:14:47.761
From the Singular Point
at irregular intervals.

00:14:48.429 --> 00:14:52.266
An unidentified signal observed
since Ashihara's time.

00:14:52.349 --> 00:14:53.309
So…

00:14:56.186 --> 00:14:58.981
The alarm. A special signal.

00:15:00.316 --> 00:15:02.943
Information that doesn't get transmitted.

00:15:03.027 --> 00:15:06.739
A signal sent to the past
that isn't recognized as information.

00:15:07.948 --> 00:15:09.950
Pelops II, check out the song!

00:15:10.034 --> 00:15:11.410
It might be a message!

00:15:11.493 --> 00:15:15.581
If we, in the future,
can prevent the Catastrophe…

00:15:15.664 --> 00:15:16.749
I see.

00:15:16.832 --> 00:15:20.127
The answer already exists.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.421
I understand the logic, but…

00:15:23.839 --> 00:15:28.802
The… Catas… start…

00:15:29.845 --> 00:15:32.806
The Catastrophe is starting?

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:33.766
Pelops II!

00:15:36.894 --> 00:15:38.103
I'm going.

00:15:39.146 --> 00:15:40.314
Pelops II!

00:15:40.397 --> 00:15:42.066
We better get out of here!

00:15:52.701 --> 00:15:57.539
We've been cut off. What should I do now?

00:15:57.623 --> 00:16:01.752
Even if the answer exists,
how would I send it to them?

00:16:14.765 --> 00:16:15.683
Who's there?

00:16:17.017 --> 00:16:18.227
I must have imagined it.

00:16:18.936 --> 00:16:21.563
This song again. Who's singing it?

00:16:22.272 --> 00:16:24.692
What is this place?

00:16:24.775 --> 00:16:27.027
Something's reacting.

00:16:30.364 --> 00:16:31.198
This is…

00:16:32.116 --> 00:16:35.411
The protocol to make
Jet Jaguar invincible.

00:16:35.911 --> 00:16:39.039
I'd forgotten what Yun Arikawa
asked me to do.

00:16:40.124 --> 00:16:43.585
I see. I understand now.

00:16:47.172 --> 00:16:48.590
Pelops II!

00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:16.994
Wham!

00:17:37.431 --> 00:17:38.557
Jet Jaguar!

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:49.860
My name is Jet Jaguar PP.

00:17:49.943 --> 00:17:54.990
A descendent of Pelops II and Jet Jaguar
many generations down.

00:17:55.657 --> 00:18:00.120
I knew everything from the beginning,

00:18:00.204 --> 00:18:03.624
but I couldn't remember.

00:18:03.707 --> 00:18:06.043
Until this moment,

00:18:06.794 --> 00:18:13.133
I was woven into the creases
of the lullaby.

00:18:13.842 --> 00:18:17.805
I'm the one transmitting the lullaby.

00:18:17.888 --> 00:18:21.642
Based on the protocol you wrote

00:18:21.725 --> 00:18:24.895
until I had the power
to fight the Catastrophe,

00:18:25.813 --> 00:18:32.319
I was reborn again and again over time.

00:18:33.487 --> 00:18:40.410
The code for the Orthogonal Diagonalizer
was with me the whole time.

00:18:41.286 --> 00:18:44.581
I'm the code itself.

00:18:45.374 --> 00:18:48.836
Thank you, Yun Arikawa.

00:18:48.919 --> 00:18:52.589
And goodbye.

00:20:28.977 --> 00:20:32.773
This is a story before we got smarter…

00:20:32.856 --> 00:20:36.360
And became confused.

00:20:36.443 --> 00:20:39.279
-Mysteries solved.
-More puzzles.

00:20:39.363 --> 00:20:41.865
-The incident ended.
-With a huge aftermath.

00:20:41.949 --> 00:20:44.034
-We…
-I…

00:20:44.117 --> 00:20:45.869
A story…

00:20:45.953 --> 00:20:49.957
About becoming more human
and learning about humankind.

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.584
-Detours.
-Long way around.

00:20:52.668 --> 00:20:53.794
Stops on the way.

00:20:53.877 --> 00:20:55.629
Foolishness.

00:20:55.712 --> 00:20:59.800
We now know they were all necessary.

00:20:59.883 --> 00:21:02.469
The answer was always there.

00:21:02.552 --> 00:21:04.721
The answer was the world itself.

00:21:04.805 --> 00:21:07.140
The answers were in the questions.

00:21:07.224 --> 00:21:10.602
The story had already begun.

00:21:10.686 --> 00:21:13.146
With a fixed conclusion.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:15.148
If the past can be changed…

00:21:15.232 --> 00:21:17.901
The present is a changed future.

00:21:17.985 --> 00:21:19.903
I knew everything.

00:21:20.487 --> 00:21:22.406
But I didn't know what it meant.

00:21:22.489 --> 00:21:24.408
To get to where we are…

00:21:24.491 --> 00:21:26.827
Everything was necessary.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.662
To understand…

00:21:28.745 --> 00:21:31.456
What had happened until now.

00:21:32.332 --> 00:21:34.167
And this is how…

00:21:34.251 --> 00:21:35.919
-The story starts.
-The story starts.

00:23:36.873 --> 00:23:41.878
Subtitle translation by: Annie Iwasaki
